rts in the same spots — a genuine sign-extension bug (accepting negative bytes) and `& 0x1` (which *does* drop a live bit) — and both are caught. So the two survivors are truncation/equivalence, not blind spots.\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified (the interposer lives in `translation/tests/fixtures/`). Full write-up in `translation/VERIFICATION.md`.","ttft_ms":2776,"ttft_stream_ms":2607,"time_to_request_ms":40,"type":"result","duration_ms":1067206,"uuid":"31a164b3-8ce3-45e9-9319-d5f308a6a9c6","queued_turn_count":0}
